<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5" extension="2015-08-01"/><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.5.1" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Progressive weakness and loss of coordination for about a year: fumbling with buttons and a bat, tripping on curbs, a fall on the ice in the winter, muscle cramps and twitching in the arms and thighs; no numbness, pain, double vision, or trouble speaking or swallowing. Examination: wasting of the hand muscles (left more than right), fasciculations in both arms and thighs, weakness of grip and of left ankle dorsiflexion, brisk reflexes with spread and a positive Hoffmann sign, normal sensation. Mixed upper and lower motor neuron signs; evaluation for motor neuron disease and its mimics begun, with neuromuscular neurology consultation booked</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M62.81</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented decline in 1938 and 1939; superseded by the diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, limb onset: progressive weakness for about a year with upper and lower motor neuron signs in the cervical and lumbosacral regions, and active and chronic denervation on EMG in the cervical, thoracic and lumbosacral regions with normal sensory nerve conduction; MRI of the brain and cervical spine and blood tests exclude mimics. Meets the Gold Coast criteria and the revised El Escorial category of clinically probable ALS. ALSFRS-R 42 and FVC 88% of predicted at diagnosis. Synthetic modern episode linked to his documented diagnosis</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G12.21</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; the documented 1939 diagnosis is the anchor. EMG findings, scores and timing are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Sprain of the left lateral ankle ligaments after tripping on a curb with left foot drop, while not wearing his ankle-foot orthosis: swelling and tenderness over the anterior talofibular ligament, able to bear weight, no bony tenderness by the Ottawa ankle rules; resolved</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>S93.402A</td><td>S — Synthetic injury; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

