<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated for a 36-year-old man with ALS. Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines given, as neuromuscular disease raises the risk from respiratory infections. He has no record of hepatitis B vaccination, so the series starts today with a screening test. He agreed to a once-in-a-lifetime hepatitis C test. [S]<list><item>Influenza, COVID-19 and first HepB-CpG vaccines today; second HepB-CpG dose in one month.</item><item>Hepatitis B triple panel and hepatitis C antibody today.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (G12.21)</content>. Slow progression with early bulbar symptoms; breathing tests next month at the ALS clinic visit. [S]<list><item>Continue riluzole and the multidisciplinary clinic plan.</item><item>Advance care planning recorded today.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/74 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 tracked at ALS clinic visits</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 2, below the risk threshold</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Overweight at intake (BMI 26.7); A1c 5.2% in May; repeat in three years</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative in May as part of the evaluation of his weakness</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Never tested; once-in-a-lifetime antibody test drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening and vaccination</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Triple panel drawn today; HepB-CpG series started</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at age 45; no family history known</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>ALS is not among the risk conditions for pneumococcal vaccination at his age on the CDC schedule; to be reviewed with the ALS clinic as respiratory muscle weakness progresses</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap four years ago after a spike wound</td></tr><tr><td>Fall prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Orthosis outdoors, cane, stair rails; physical therapy home program</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season (inactivated); COVID-19 vaccine, 2026-2027 formula; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), first of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis B and C results by phone. ALS clinic and primary care visit in four weeks with breathing tests; second hepatitis B vaccine dose then. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-19: five months after diagnosis: breathing tests and noninvasive ventilation planning, nutrition and gastrostomy discussion, and his new desk work. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 30 minutes, early in his illness as he asked, with his consent. He named a health care agent, recorded in the confidential part of the chart and not named here. He wants to be told plainly how his illness is changing and to make his own decisions. He would accept noninvasive ventilation when it is needed and would consider a feeding tube if eating became unsafe or his weight fell. He has not decided about a tracheostomy and long-term ventilation and wants to learn more from the ALS clinic before deciding. He chose to wait before completing a portable medical order form. To be revisited at each ALS clinic visit and with any change in breathing or swallowing. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
